  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p&gt;The proposal will fail to provide adequate provision for on-site cycle storage facilities and therefore fails to promote sustainable methods of transport. This is contrary to the aims of Policies 20 and 61 of the adopted Waltham Forest Local Plan LP1 (2024), which seek to encourage a shift towards sustainable modes of transport for occupiers.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;The scheme will represent a substandard level of accommodation for occupiers in that bedroom 2 at ground-floor level fails to meet the Council&#x27;s minimum HMO space standards to constitute a bedroom. This will be harmful to the living conditions of the occupier, to the detriment of continued enjoyment, and therefore fails to comply with the amenity objectives of Policies 20 and 57 of the adopted Waltham Forest Local Plan LP1 (2024).&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;In the absence of a legal agreement, the proposal fails to provide the necessary financial contributions to secure adequate mitigation against the Epping Forest Special Area of Conservation. It therefore fails to comply with Policy 81 of the adopted Waltham Forest Local Plan LP1 (2024) and the Supplementary Planning Document - Planning Obligations (2017).&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;In the absence of a legal agreement to restrict occupiers in obtaining on-street parking permits, the proposal constitutes unsustainable development in that it does not promote sustainable transport, which conflicts with the objectives of Policies 60 and 66 of the adopted Waltham Forest Local Plan LP1 (2024).&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
